---
import EditorialFrame from '../../components/EditorialFrame.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import { services, fmtDate, humanValue } from '../../lib/data.js';
import { newestDate } from '../../lib/editorial.js';

const svc = services.CA.get('visitor-visa');
const ok = svc.records.filter(r => r.status === 'ok');
const fastest = ok.slice(0, 10);
const slowest = ok.slice(-10).reverse();
const median = Math.round(svc.medianDays);
const big = ['IN', 'NG', 'PH', 'PK', 'CN', 'BR', 'MX', 'BD', 'VN', 'CO']
  .map(cc => ok.find(r => r.applicant_country === cc)).filter(Boolean);
const citations = [...new Set(svc.records.map(record => record.source_url))];
---
<EditorialFrame sectionName="Guides" sectionPath="/guides/" slug="canada-visitor-visa-by-country"
  title={`Canada visitor visa times by country — ${median}-day median`}
  description={`Compare current IRCC visitor-visa times by country: ${median}-day median, fastest and slowest routes, major corridors, official sources and history.`}
  h1="Canada visitor visa times, analyzed by country"
  lede={`IRCC currently publishes visitor-visa processing times for ${ok.length} applicant countries (of ${svc.records.length} tracked). The median is ${median} days, while current published values run from ${fastest[0].value_raw} to ${slowest[0].value_raw}. Data as of ${fmtDate(svc.latestEffective)}.`}
  published="2026-08-22" modified={newestDate('2026-08-23', svc.latestEffective)} checked={svc.latestEffective}
  about={['Canada visitor visa', 'IRCC processing times']} citations={citations} adPrefix="guide-ca-visitor-compare">
  <AdSlot position="guide-top" />

  <h2>Major corridors right now</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Applying from</th><th>Official time</th><th>vs. typical</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {big.map(r => (
        <tr>
          <td><a href={`/canada/visitor-visa/${r.applicantSlug}/`}>{r.applicant_country_name}</a></td>
          <td class="num">{humanValue(r)}</td>
          <td>{r.speed ? <span class={`chip ${r.speed.cls}`}>{r.speed.label}</span> : '—'}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>The ten shortest currently published times</h2>
  <div class="related">
    {fastest.map(r => <a href={`/canada/visitor-visa/${r.applicantSlug}/`}>{r.applicant_country_name}: <strong class="num">&nbsp;{r.value_raw}</strong></a>)}
  </div>
  <p>IRCC does not publish the route-level sample size or a reason beside each country value. The ranking therefore shows only the current processing-time statistic; it cannot establish capacity, approval likelihood or why one country is shorter.</p>

  <h2>The ten slowest</h2>
  <div class="related">
    {slowest.map(r => <a href={`/canada/visitor-visa/${r.applicantSlug}/`}>{r.applicant_country_name}: <strong class="num">&nbsp;{r.value_raw}</strong></a>)}
  </div>
  <p>A longer country value calls for more planning room, but it does not identify the cause. IRCC lists completeness, verification, response time, application volume and complexity among factors that can affect a wait. Watch the dated route history instead of relying on an undated screenshot.</p>

  <h2>Read the movement, not just the level</h2>
  <p>Because IRCC recalculates weekly from completed cases, each route's history (which we record and the official site does not keep) tells you whether a corridor is clearing or clogging. Every country page on this site shows that history alongside today's figure — see <a href="/canada/visitor-visa/">the full table of all {svc.records.length} countries</a>.</p>

  <div class="prov">Computed from the tracked dataset at build time; updates automatically with every refresh. Source: IRCC. Not legal advice.</div>
  <AdSlot position="guide-bottom" />
</EditorialFrame>
